<!--
NODrugLung.DES - Defines lung metabolism and clearance of NO in HumMod

Overview
This file models the **metabolism and clearance of Nitric Oxide (NO) in the lungs, focusing on:
1. Bioavailability of NO: How much NO remains available after passing through the lungs.
2. Permeability Calculation: Determines how effectively NO crosses the lung barrier into systemic circulation.
3. Clearance Dynamics: Tracks the rate at which NO is lost from the lungs over time.

1. Defines Drug Availability: Uses `BIOAVAIL = 0.6` to specify that 60% of the inhaled NO is available after degradation.
2. Models Lung Permeability: Uses `PERM = 0.1` to control how quickly NO crosses the lung barrier**.
3. Calculates Drug Loss: Determines NO loss rate and its conversion to micromolar units.

How to Replicate for Another Drug
1. Change `<name> NODrugLung </name>` to `<name> NewDrugLung </name>`.
2. Adjust BIOAVAIL to match the new drug’s lung absorption properties.
3. Modify PERM to reflect the drug’s permeability in the lungs.

-->

HumMod / IsoproterenolLung

Created : 25-Jul-13
Last Modified : 
Author : W Pruett
Copyright : 2006-2013
By : University Of Mississippi Medical Center
Schema : DES V1.0

<structure><name> NODrugLung </name> <!-- Defines NO metabolism and clearance in the lungs -->

<variables>

<constant>
  <name> BIOAVAIL </name> <!-- Fraction of drug that enters the lungs after inhalation -->
  <val> 0.6 </val> <!-- 60% remains available after degradation -->
</constant>

<constant>
  <name> PERM </name> <!-- Permeability factor of NO across lung tissue -->
  <val> 0.1 </val> <!-- Lower value between 0-1 indicates slower permeability. adjust based on the drug! -->
</constant>

<var>
  <name> Loss </name> <!-- Tracks rate of NO loss from the lungs -->
</var>

<var>
  <name> Loss(umol) </name> <!-- Loss converted into micromolar units -->
</var>

</variables>

<equations>

<diffeq>
  <name> Mass </name> <!-- Tracks current NO mass in the lungs -->
  <integralname> Mass </integralname>
  <initialval> 0.0 </initialval> <!-- Starts with no NO in the lungs -->
  <dervname> Change </dervname>
  <errorlim> 0.01 </errorlim> <!-- Controls integration error tolerance. See previous note about judging tolerance limit in prevous files. -->
</diffeq>

</equations>

<definitions>

<block><name> Dervs </name> <!-- Defines NO clearance and absorption dynamics -->

<def>
  <name> Loss </name>
  <val> BIOAVAIL * PERM * Mass </val> <!-- Computes NO loss based on lung availability and permeability -->
</def>

<def>
  <name> Loss(umol) </name>
  <val> Loss / NODrugPool.MW </val> <!-- Converts NO loss into micromolar concentration -->
</def>

<def>
  <name> Change </name>
  <val> - Loss / BIOAVAIL </val> <!-- Defines rate of NO clearance from the lungs -->
</def>

</block>

</definitions>
</structure>

End
